er gate maps whose content nothing pins:**\n79|\n80|| Table | Site | Consequence |\n81||---|---|---|\n82|| `successMembers` | protocol.go:370 | success envelope admits an extra member (**confirmed**) |\n83|| `failureMembers` | protocol.go:460 | failure envelope admits an extra member |\n84|| `manifestMembers` | manifest.go:119 | manifest admits an extra member; the census local shadows the package var |\n85|| `doctorResultMembers` | probe.go:584 | doctor result admits an extra member |\n86|\n87|Bypass probe: with `successMembers` widened by one name, a frame carrying\n88|`ax.planted.member` is **ADMITTED** by `CheckSuccessEnvelope`; the unwidened\n89|control refuses it (`PROBE-REFUSED`).\n90|\n91|## Batch 5 — F3/F5/F6/F7 closure: 17 of 17 killed\n92|\n93|| ID | Narrows | Result | Named failing test |\n94||---|---|---|---|\n95|| F3a | `second > 0xDFFF` → `> 0xDFFF+1` | KILLED | TestSurrogatePairSweep |\n96|| F3b | `second < 0xDC00` → `< 0xDBFF` | KILLED | TestSurrogatePairSweep |\n97|| F3c | `second > 0xDFFF` → `>= 0xDFFF` (refuses a valid pair) | KILLED | TestSurrogatePairSweep |\n98|| F3d | `second < 0xDC00` → `<= 0xDC00` (refuses a valid pair) | KILLED | TestSurrogatePairSweep |\n99|| F3e | `first <= 0xDBFF` → `<= 0xDBFE` | KILLED | TestLoneSurrogateSweep, TestSurrogatePairSweep |\n100|| F5a | echo narrowed to length-only | KILLED | TestCheckContextEcho |\n101|| F5b | echo narrowed to a 32-byte prefix | KILLED | TestCheckContextEcho |\n102|| F6a–f | frame bound `> Max+1` and `>= Max` on request, success, failure | KILLED ×6 | TestFrameBoundEdges/{request,success,failure}/{exact_bound,one_over} |\n103|| F7a | provider equality exempts the zero fact | KILLED | TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse |\n104|| F7b | environment equality exempts the zero fact | KILLED | TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse |\n105|| F7c | candidate-kind equality exempts the zero fact | KILLED | TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse |\n106|| F7d | validate mode echo exempts the zero fact | KILLED | TestValidateResultRules/zero_request_mode_fact |\n107|\n108|Excluded as equivalent: dropping `secondLength < 0` is subsumed by the following\n109|range test (`second == 0 < 0xDC00`), so no input distinguishes it.\n110|\n111|## Batch 6 — resurrection sweep over round-1 kills: 12 of 12 killed\n112|\n113|| ID | Narrows | Result |\n114||---|---|---|\n115|| R1–R8 | `CheckBindingEquality` drops each of the eight identity facts | KILLED ×8 (TestBindingEqualityFlipsEveryFact) |\n116|| R9 | `checkStringBounds` max → `maximum+1` | KILLED |\n117|| R10 | `checkStringBounds` min → `minimum-1` | KILLED |\n118|| R11 | `checkUint53Bounds` max → `maximum+1` | KILLED |\n119|| R12 | `checkUint53Bounds` min → `minimum+1` | KILLED |\n120|\n121|## Batch 7 — `CheckCallBinding` zero-fact exemptions: 0 of 5 killed\n122|\n123|| Gate | Result |\n124||---|---|\n125|| `role != binding.Role` exempts `binding.Role == \"\"` | **SURVIVED** |\n126|| `context.ProviderID != binding.ProviderID` exempts the zero fact | **SURVIVED** |\n127|| `context.ManifestDigest != binding.AdapterManifestDigest` exempts the zero fact | **SURVIVED** |\n128|| `context.ExecutableSHA256 != binding.ExecutableSHA256` exempts the zero fact | **SURVIVED** |\n129|| `context.Environment != admitted` exempts the zero tuple | **SURVIVED** |\n130|\n131|## Open-class bound (not counted in the ratio)\n132|\n133|`unknownMember` exempting `\"debug\"` and exempting `\"ax.planted.member\"` both\n134|SURVIVE. This is the F8 bound the inventory header records explicitly; the reject\n135|class is unbounded, so no single narrowing mutant is decisive. Correctly declared,\n136|not a finding.\n137|\n138|## Behavioural probes (not mutants)\n139|\n140|| Probe | Result |\n141||---|---|\n142|| archive-mode validate success through `CheckSuccessBody` with the package's own fixtures | **REFUSED**: `validate archive mode carries a target member` (member `projection_plan_id`) — finding B1 |\n143|| success envelope carrying an extra member, `successMembers` unwidened (control) | refused |\n144|| success envelope carrying an extra member, `successMembers` widened by one | **ADMITTED** — finding B2 |\n145|\n146|## Method bounds\n147|\n148|- Measures gates reachable from this package's exported API. No in-repo caller\n149|  sequences `Discover → CheckProbe → CheckTupleAdmission → CheckCallBinding`;\n150|  nothing outside `internal/sessadapter` imports the package.\n151|- Does not attack `internal/canonicaljson`, `internal/scalar`, or `internal/axerror`,\n152|  which several gates delegate to.\n153|- The census shape probes measure syntactic visibility, not reachability: a planted\n154|  vocabulary is consulted live but its verdict is behaviour-neutral by construction,\n155|  which is what isolates the census from the behavioural suite.\n156|- Three of the four unpinned `*Members` maps are reported as unpinned by identical\n157|  construction, not as four separate bypass probes; one was confirmed behaviourally."}}}
