{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07450-f188-71b1-8e87-3b58e1805190"},"sequence":200,"recorded_at":1780531400000395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141"},"call_id":"call_01a074519735740386fd97c13c579e38","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2z3se0/TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2z3se0 — rework evidence rev2 (answers review-verdict-rev1)\n2|\n3|- Tree: worktree `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3drr2m`, all changes inside\n4|  `internal/sessadapter/` (production + tests). Previously reviewed files\n5|  (`LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`, `internal/traceability/*`) untouched.\n6|- Method from the verdict brief was followed: every mutant below was confirmed\n7|  PRESENT (grep after patch) and compiling (`go vet` exit 0) before its\n8|  red/green was believed; compile failures would not count as kills.\n9|  Production restored after every mutant (full suite re-run green at the end).\n10|- Battery log: `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-battery-rev2.log` (27 lines, one per\n11|  mutant, with compile + red flags).\n12|\n13|## What was done per finding\n14|\n15|### F1 — census blind to non-table vocabularies (blocking)\n16|Production: all nine inline unions converted to table loops with `valid*`\n17|consultants (refusal call sites and detail strings byte-identical, so the\n18|323-arm inventory is unchanged):\n19|`objectModes`/`validObjectMode` (context.go), `directionNames`/`validDirection`,\n20|`tupleEntryStatuses`/`validTupleEntryStatus`, `evidenceResults`/\n21|`validEvidenceResult`, `candidateKindNames`/`validCandidateKind`,\n22|`contextFreeOperations`/`operationSkipsRequestContext` (tuple.go,\n23|operations.go), `registryEntryStatuses`/`validRegistryEntryStatus` (probe.go),\n24|`roleNames`/`validRole` (discovery.go). The last three (candidate kind, role,\n25|context-free dispatch) are the same shape the detector found beyond the five\n26|named in the verdict.\n27|Census: `scanVocabularyTables` now resolves named slice/map types package-wide\n28|(`type s []string` + `var t = s{...}` is a table; struct literals are not);\n29|new `TestNoUnregisteredInlineVocabularies` forbids any boolean chain comparing\n30|one operand against 2+ closed values (literals, constants, conversions);\n31|header comment rewritten to state exactly what the scanner sees plus the\n32|syntactic-scanner bound. Registrations 55 → 63.\n33|Spec pins (`TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`): object modes, tuple entry\n34|statuses, registry entry statuses, evidence results (both sentences),\n35|context-free operations (derived no-context set), doctor directions, key\n36|directions/roles/candidate kinds now pin the production tables (previously\n37|literals where they existed at all).\n38|Killed by: M01–M09 (table widenings + chain reintroduction).\n39|\n40|### F2 — `var x = ctor` alias hole (blocking)\n41|`collectFileArms` (inventory_test.go) now exempts only the definition's own\n42|Name in its ValueSpec; a constructor in value position fails the file in all\n43|three spellings. Doc comment states the exact rule. Regression:\n44|`TestConstructorAliasSpellingsFailDerivation` (control + definition-exempt +\n45|three alias probes on synthetic sources). 323/323 maintained.\n46|Killed by: M11 (package-level var alias → derivation error\n47|`constructor alias of failInvalid buries every arm it builds at ...:3:19`),\n48|M12 (function-local var alias → derivation error), M13 control (direct-call\n49|planted arm derives and is reported unwitnessed\n50|`ctor|failInvalid|planted direct arm`).\n51|\n52|### F3 — surrogate pairing bound (blocking)\n53|New `TestSurrogatePairSweep`: every high surrogate (1024) × {lowLo−1, lowLo,\n54|lowHi, lowHi+1} in upper hex, lowercase edge spot checks, full low-range sweep\n55|for first/middle/last high. Verdicts from test-local range literals\n56|(`lowLo=0xDC00, lowHi=0xDFFF`), never from production constants: 2058 refused\n57|+ 5124 admitted.\n58|Killed by: M14 (`second > 0xDFFF+1` admits `A\\uD800\\uE000B`), M15\n59|(`second < 0xDBFF` admits `A\\uD800\\uDBFFB`).\n60|\n61|### F4 — set-valued gates proven on a sample (blocking)\n62|- `TestCheckDoctorHealthyDrivesEveryRequiredCapability` (probe_test.go):\n63|  required set derived from `DoctorRequiredCapabilities` (both writer\n64|  variants, count pinned at 4), whole-set pass + each member weakened alone\n65|  refusing naming that member (8 subtests).\n66|- `TestCheckValidateNullabilityDrivesEveryTarget`\n67|  (operations_semantic_test.go): archive-carry and staged-miss per member\n68|  through `CheckRequestBody` (8 refusal subtests + 2 passes). Obligation list\n69|  written in-test so a narrowed production list reddens instead of shrinking\n70|  the probe; names cross-pinned by the member census + operation table.\n71|- `TestCheckValidateResultDrivesEveryApplicableCheck`: each of the three\n72|  applicable checks false under valid=true refuses naming it, plus a garbage\n73|  (`\"yes\"`) per-member type case.\n74|Killed by: M16 (required[:1]), M17/M18 (targets[:3] both branches), M19\n75|(applicable drop), M20 (nullable-bool drop, killed via arm slide\n76|`not a boolean` → `failed applicable check`).\n77|\n78|### F5 — same-length context forgery\n79|`TestCheckContextEcho` gains a same-length case: one flipped hex digit in\n80|`operation_id` (length asserted equal, `DecodeCallContext` asserted valid, so\n81|the verdict isolates the echo gate), refused `byte-for-byte`.\n82|Killed by: M21 (echo narrowed to length-only).\n83|\n84|### F6 — 8 MiB edges\n85|New `TestFrameBoundEdges`: frames of exactly `MaxFrameBytes` (must fail on\n86|content, never on length) and `MaxFrameBytes+1` (must fail\n87|`exceeds the 8 MiB bound`) through all three entry points\n88|(`DecodeRequestFrame`, `CheckSuccessEnvelope`, `CheckFailureEnvelope`).\n89|Killed by: M22 (`> MaxFrameBytes+1`), M23 (`>= MaxFrameBytes`).\n90|\n91|### F7 — zero-value host facts\n92|New `TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse` (3 subtests) + `TestValidateResultRules/\n93|zero_request_mode_fact`: each zero fact with a non-empty probe side refuses\n94|through its own arm.\n95|Killed by: M24–M27 (zero-guards on the four equalities; M24 kills via arm\n96|slide `requested provider` → `verified manifest`).\n97|\n98|### F8 — open-class gates\n99|Recorded as a stated bound in the inventory header (unknown/duplicate-member\n100|gates range over an unbounded name class; one witness per arm proves the gate\n101|fires, not that every name is gated). No code change, as directed.\n102|\n103|## Mutant battery (narrowing unless noted; 26 killed + 1 control-green / 27)\n104|\n105|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named test that fails | Result |\n106||---|---|---|---|\n107|| M01 objectModes+reuse_sink | admit one extra mode | TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec | KILLED |\n108|| M02 tupleEntryStatuses+expired | admit one extra status | TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec | KILLED |\n109|| M03 evidenceResults+waived | admit one extra result | TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec | KILLED |\n110|| M04 directionNames+hybrid | admit one extra direction | TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec | KILLED |\n111|| M05 registryEntryStatuses+pending | admit one extra status | TestDoctorResultRules | KILLED |\n112|| M06 roleNames+spectator | admit one extra role | TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec | KILLED |\n113|| M07 candidateKindNames+sidecar | admit one extra kind | TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec | KILLED |\n114|| M08 contextFreeOperations+OpDoctor | skip context for one more op | TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec | KILLED |\n115|| M09 inline `direction!=\"source_read\"&&!=...` reintroduced (behavior identical) | shape gate, not behavior | TestNoUnregisteredInlineVocabularies | KILLED |\n116|| M10 named-type table spelling | visibility control, must stay green | TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered | CONTROL-GREEN |\n117|| M11 `var plantedFail=failInvalid` + arm | hide every arm built through it | TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (derivation error) | KILLED |\n118|| M12 function-local `var localFail=failInvalid` + arm | same, local spelling | TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (derivation error) | KILLED |\n119|| M13 direct-call planted arm | control: derivation must see it | TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed (unwitnessed arm) | KILLED |\n120|| M14 `second>0xDFFF`→`>0xDFFF+1` | admit U+E000 after high | TestSurrogatePairSweep | KILLED |\n121|| M15 `second<0xDC00`→`<0xDBFF` | admit high-after-high | TestSurrogatePairSweep | KILLED |\n122|| M16 doctor `required[:1]` | check 1 of 4 capabilities | TestCheckDoctorHealthyDrivesEveryRequiredCapability | KILLED |\n123|| M17 nullability archive `targets[:3]` | check 3 of 4 targets | TestCheckValidateNullabilityDrivesEveryTarget | KILLED |\n124|| M18 nullability staged `targets[:3]` | check 3 of 4 targets | TestCheckValidateNullabilityDrivesEveryTarget | KILLED |\n125|| M19 applicable loop drops resume_surface_valid | admit false check | TestCheckValidateResultDrivesEveryApplicableCheck | KILLED |\n126|| M20 nullable-bool loop drops resume_surface_valid | admit non-bool member | TestCheckValidateResultDrivesEveryApplicableCheck (arm slide) | KILLED |\n127|| M21 echo `&& len!=len` | admit same-length forgery | TestCheckContextEcho | KILLED |\n128|| M22 request `>MaxFrameBytes+1` | admit 8 MiB+1 frame | TestFrameBoundEdges | KILLED |\n129|| M23 request `>=MaxFrameBytes` | refuse the exact edge | TestFrameBoundEdges | KILLED |\n130|| M24 provider equality `&& ExpectedProviderID!=\"\"` | admit on zero fact | TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse (arm slide) | KILLED |\n131|| M25 env equality `&& Manifest.EnvironmentID!=\"\"` | admit on zero fact | TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse | KILLED |\n132|| M26 kind equality `&& expectedKind!=\"\"` | admit on zero fact | TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse | KILLED |\n133|| M27 mode echo `&& ValidateMode!=\"\"` | admit on zero fact | TestValidateResultRules/zero_request_mode_fact | KILLED |\n134|\n135|Survivors: none. Every survivor class from rev1 is measured above and killed.\n136|Method bounds (what this battery cannot see): no in-repo caller sequences\n137|`Discover → CheckProbe → CheckTupleAdmission → CheckCallBinding` (package has\n138|no in-repo importers); delegated packages (`canonicaljson`, `scalar`,\n139|`axerror`) not attacked; runtime-built sets would evade the syntactic census\n140|(none exist — every table is a package-level composite the scan pins);\n141|open-class member gates per the F8 bound; map-iteration determinism is held by\n142|single-unknown fixtures, and the suite was run `-count=3` green.\n143|\n144|## AC coverage: 10 of 11 rows driven through production entry points\n145|\n146|| AC row | Production call site | Named committed test |\n147||---|---|---|\n148|| discovery | Discover (discovery.go) | TestDiscoverBindsManifestToCandidate (+ role table via TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec/roles) |\n149|| manifest | DecodeManifest (manifest.go) | TestDecodeManifestAcceptsFixture |\n150|| probe | DecodeProbe/CheckProbe (probe.go) | TestDecodeProbeAcceptsFixture, TestCheckProbe*, TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse |\n151|| closed operations | CheckRequestBody/CheckSuccessBody (operations.go) | TestEveryOperationHasContractVectors (+ per-op semantic tests) |\n152|| limits | DecodeResourceLimits (context.go) | TestDecodeResourceLimitsBounds |\n153|| idempotency | VerifyRequestDigest + CheckContextEcho (context.go) | TestRequestDigestFixpoint, TestCheckContextEcho (now with same-length forgery) |\n154|| tuple gates | CheckTupleAdmission + entry/key decoders (tuple.go) | TestCheckTupleAdmissionRefusals (+ entry-status/result/dir pins) |\n155|| exact fixtures | fixture acceptance tests | TestDecodeManifestAcceptsFixture, TestDecodeProbeAcceptsFixture, contract vectors |\n156|| negative/refusal | all refusal constructors | TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry (323/323) + per-gate negatives above |\n157|| no unsupported capability | CheckTargetWriteGates, DoctorRequiredCapabilities | TestCheckTargetWriteGates, TestDoctorRequiredCapabilities, TestCheckDoctorHealthyDrivesEveryRequiredCapability |\n158|| crash/idempotency-durable-state evidence | N/A by stated bound | package mutates no durable state (doc.go); no crash-evidence row applicable |\n159|\n160|## Anomaly found during F4 (behavior preserved, reported, not redesigned)\n161|\n162|`checkValidateNullability` is shared by request and success bodies, but\n163|validate success bodies carry no target members and the member set is exact,\n164|so an archive-mode success is ALWAYS refused (`carries a target member` on\n165|absent members — reproduced with a scratch test, then removed), while a\n166|staged/live success always passes nullability vacuously. The success-side\n167|call is therefore a mode gate in disguise, not a nullability check. F4\n168|coverage is driven request-side (both branches × 4 members) where the rule is\n169|well-defined. Fix options: (a) scope the rule to request bodies; (b) treat\n170|absent as null on success (breaks staged successes — needs a wider redesign);\n171|(c) declare archive success impossible. Needs a product/spec decision — left\n172|for review, recorded in LOGBOOK.md. No behavior changed.\n173|\n174|## Gates (exit codes observed directly, no pipes)\n175|\n176|- `go test ./... -count=1`: 17/17 packages ok, exit 0\n177|- `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -v -count=1`: 904 PASS, 0 FAIL, exit 0\n178|- `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=3`: ok, exit 0\n179|- `go test -race ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1`: ok, exit 0\n180|- `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -cover`: 81.4% of statements (was 81.1%)\n181|- `go vet ./internal/sessadapter/`: exit 0; `GOOS=windows go vet`: exit 0\n182|- `gofmt -l internal/sessadapter/`: empty\n183|- Mutant battery `/tmp/mutant-battery.py`: 26 killed + 1 control-green / 27,\n184|  every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
