{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7dd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07450-f188-71b1-8e87-3b58e1805190"},"sequence":585,"recorded_at":1780531400001165,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"c8b204b4-6808-4393-aae3-11d91d65a9db"},"task_id":"c8b204b4-6808-4393-aae3-11d91d65a9db","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"c8b204b4-6808-4393-aae3-11d91d65a9db","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-13-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"CheckCallBinding\\\" internal/sessadapter/*_test.go | head -n 20\\necho ===\\ngrep -rn \\\"TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse\\\" internal/sessadapter/*_test.go | head\\necho ===\\ngrep -n \\\"archive\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Find binding tests and logbook anomaly\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"internal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:103:func TestCheckCallBinding(t *testing.T) {\\ninternal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:121:\\tif err := CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, context, admitted); err != nil {\\ninternal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:122:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"CheckCallBinding: %v\\\", err)\\ninternal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:124:\\tif err := CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleTarget, context, admitted); err == nil {\\ninternal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:131:\\tif err := CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, foreignProvider, admitted); err == nil {\\ninternal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:138:\\tif err := CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, foreignManifest, admitted); err == nil {\\ninternal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:145:\\tif err := CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, foreignExe, admitted); err == nil {\\ninternal/sessadapter/discovery_test.go:152:\\tif err := CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, context, otherTuple); err == nil {\\ninternal/sessadapter/inventory_witnesses_test.go:1475:\\t\\t\\trequireRefusal(t, CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, context, other), \\\"unsupported_environment_tuple\\\", \\\"environment\\\", fixtureEnvironmentID, \\\"admitted tuple\\\")\\ninternal/sessadapter/inventory_witnesses_test.go:1505:\\t\\t\\trequireRefusal(t, CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleTarget, context, admitted), \\\"integrity_failure\\\", \\\"subject\\\", \\\"role\\\", \\\"binding role\\\")\\ninternal/sessadapter/inventory_witnesses_test.go:1511:\\t\\t\\trequireRefusal(t, CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, context, admitted), \\\"integrity_failure\\\", \\\"subject\\\", \\\"provider_id\\\", \\\"sealed binding\\\")\\ninternal/sessadapter/inventory_witnesses_test.go:1517:\\t\\t\\trequireRefusal(t, CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, context, admitted), \\\"integrity_failure\\\", \\\"subject\\\", \\\"session_adapter_manifest_digest\\\", \\\"sealed binding\\\")\\ninternal/sessadapter/inventory_witnesses_test.go:1523:\\t\\t\\trequireRefusal(t, CheckCallBinding(binding, RoleSource, context, admitted), \\\"integrity_failure\\\", \\\"subject\\\", \\\"executable_sha256\\\", \\\"sealed binding\\\")\\n===\\ninternal/sessadapter/probe_test.go:240:// TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse pins the fail-closed half of the\\ninternal/sessadapter/probe_test.go:247:func TestZeroValueHostFactsRefuse(t *testing.T) {\\n===\\n17:- ANOMALY (behavior preserved, needs product decision): `checkValidateNullability` is shared by request and success bodies, but validate success bodies carry no target members and the member set is exact, so archive-mode success ALWAYS refuses (`carries a target member` on absent members, reproduced with a scratch test) while staged/live success passes vacuously — the success-side call is a mode gate in disguise. F4 driven request-side where the rule is well-defined. Options: scope the rule to requests / redesign absent-handling / declare archive success impossible.\\n417:- EVIDENCE: 14 sibling retargets derived from the document itself — every shared-member pair of the Section 10.4 Git table, both directions — each planted into a copy of the shipped artifact and each required to be refused by the sibling's name. Six mutants run in a throwaway `git archive` copy, all confirmed present before measurement: deleting the anchor reddens all 15 sibling and field plants; narrowing it to `Type` tables only reddens the field-table plant; restoring one of the seven pre-fix citations reddens and names the row and GitHead; removing the table-row boundary reddens both the specdoc and the artifact stitch tests; removing one declaring pin reddens 8 shipped rows rather than granting a free pass; a stale pin and a stale exemption both redden. Class re-scan over all 347 rows: 357 citations, 235 on table body rows, 0 naming another type, 2 naming another member and both exempted by name.\\n480:- STATUS: `internal/canonicaljson` 97.2% before and after, verified against a `git archive HEAD` baseline. gofmt, `go build ./...`, both cross-compile targets, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-cover -count=1`, `-race -count=1`, tracecheck, `cataloggen -check` and all five fuzz gates at 100x exit 0.\\n618:- FINDING: reproduced at the production `loadConfigDocument` entry with a 34-shape hostile-endpoint probe. Against the pre-fix base (an archive of checkpoint `10aaa16`) 32 of 34 loaded with `err=nil`, including `endpoint = \\\"-oStrictHostKeyChecking=no\\\"`, `\\\"-oUserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null\\\"`, `\\\"-F/attacker/config\\\"`, `\\\"-J jump.example\\\"`, `\\\"--\\\"`, and `\\\"peer.example -oStrictHostKeyChecking=no\\\"`. The first two are exactly the bypass Section 6.3 requires refusing, reached through a field the ssh_args gate never inspects. Only the tab and newline shapes were already refused, one clause earlier by the printable-character bound. After the fix all 34 are refused and every option-shaped one names the `option-like value` clause. Probe logs: `.temp/BUG-260902-4ajzyz/audit-probe-before-01.log` and `-after-01.log`.\\n640:- STATUS: BUG-260902-4ajzyz on `task-board/story/STORY-260902-cq7ivu`, kept to one signed commit. Reapplied from the accepted patch of BUG-260902-3c7ovg, which could not be integrated because its move chain had a cycle, then amended for both review findings above and kept to that one commit through two review cycles. `internal/config` coverage 94.4% at the base (measured from an archive copy of checkpoint `10aaa16`) -> 94.7%, unchanged by the rev2 rework, which is test-only; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l .`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `go test ./... -cover`, tracecheck (global and sections 6.1-6.5), and the catalog `-check` gate all exit 0, with no generated-file drift. Handed off to review.\\n776:- STATUS: BUG-260902-2faftr, on `task-board/story/STORY-260902-2oiugz` (forked from trunk `67aed0b`, zero commits behind `main` at measurement time); `internal/config` coverage 94.4%, against a 93.9% pre-change measurement taken from a `git archive HEAD` copy (the preservation tests raise it; no statement lost coverage); `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l ./internal`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `go test ./... -cover -count=1`, full and assigned-scope `tracecheck`, and `cataloggen -check` all exit 0; the seven single-clause mutants were re-run on this tree and each exited 1, counting `--- FAIL` subtest lines only (re-added key blacklist reddens 17 of the 20 admission subtests, reproducing the accepted review's measurement exactly; re-added nested-key blacklist 10; dropped grammar gate 11; widened 253-byte key bound 2; widened depth bound 2; dropped registered backend-settings schema call 2; dropped `DisallowUnknownFields` 5), with the tree restored green after each. An eighth mutant closes the review's non-blocking finding: deleting every blacklisted-label nested key from the loaded map passes the whole suite on the previous revision (exit 0) and reddens all 11 preservation subtests here (exit 1). With the preservation tests present the two required narrowing mutants redden more, not less: re-added key blacklist 18, re-added nested-key blacklist 21. Handed off to review. No commit hash is named here: this entry ships in the commit it would describe, so the hash cannot be known when it is written.\\n917:- FINDINGS (all verified against the raw document, each would have been a silent wrong-source derivation): the request envelope sentence exists three times (7.5-style, 7.8, 7.9) and the capability-value sentence twice (Provider Probe 7.4 vs Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\\\\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8122,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2031,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
