{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ccaf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07450-f188-71b1-8e87-3b58e1805190"},"sequence":1202,"recorded_at":1780531400002399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"acdfe288-4f4e-444a-ae51-26b969af2141"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"c60b87c1-b0bd-46d4-9d11-ad66d69da605"},"task_id":"c60b87c1-b0bd-46d4-9d11-ad66d69da605","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"c60b87c1-b0bd-46d4-9d11-ad66d69da605","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-06\n7|\n8|### 0444 — Session-adapter leaf rework: all four blocking verdict findings closed, one anomaly reported\n9|\n10|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, F1–F4 blocking + F5–F7). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/`; previously reviewed files untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n11|- FIX (F1): nine inline closed unions → table loops with `valid*` consultants (mode, direction, entry status, registry-entry status, evidence result, candidate kind, role, context-free ops). Refusal details byte-identical, 323-arm inventory unchanged. Census scanner extended two ways: named slice/map types resolve package-wide; new `TestNoUnregisteredInlineVocabularies` forbids any chain comparing one operand against 2+ closed values. The new detector immediately found two more real unions (probe candidate kind, manifest/probe context dispatch) the reviewer had not listed. Spec pins for all eight unions; registrations 55 → 63.\n12|- FIX (F2): `collectFileArms` exempts only the definition Name in its ValueSpec; `var x = ctor` fails package-level and function-local. `TestConstructorAliasSpellingsFailDerivation` replays all four probes on synthetic sources.\n13|- FIX (F3): `TestSurrogatePairSweep` — every high × {lowLo−1, lowLo, lowHi, lowHi+1} plus full-range interior for three highs, verdicts from test-local literals: 2058 refused + 5124 admitted.\n14|- FIX (F4): per-member drivers for doctor-required (4×2 writer variants), nullability (4×2 branches, request side), applicable checks (3) + nullable-bool types (3).\n15|- FIX (F5/F6/F7): same-length echo forgery; exact/over frame edges on all three envelopes; four zero-value host-fact refusals.\n16|- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 26 killed + 1 control-green / 27 measured, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict (`/tmp/mutant-battery.py`, log attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-battery-rev2.log`). Gates: `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0, sessadapter 904 PASS/0 FAIL, `-count=3` green, `-race` green, cover 81.1% → 81.4%, vet + GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean.\n17|- ANOMALY (behavior preserved, needs product decision): `checkValidateNullability` is shared by request and success bodies, but validate success bodies carry no target members and the member set is exact, so archive-mode success ALWAYS refuses (`carries a target member` on absent members, reproduced with a scratch test) while staged/live success passes vacuously — the success-side call is a mode gate in disguise. F4 driven request-side where the rule is well-defined. Options: scope the rule to requests / redesign absent-handling / declare archive success impossible.\n18|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n19|\n20|## 2026-09-05\n21|\n22|### 0935 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: switch vocabularies, ExecRunner frame loss, flake bound\n23|\n24|- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-6 verdict (changes requested, two blocking findings F1/F2 plus the nondeterministic suite). Carries the reviewer's findings into the logbook — the reviewer deliberately left LOGBOOK.md out of their delta. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n25|- FIX (F1, blocking): the three switch-shaped closed vocabularies the census could not see (envelope member set `checkResponseMembers` ← `DecodeResponse:416`, execution profile `ProfileMapping` ← `DecodeSpawnPlan:100`, transaction state `validStatusState` ← `DecodeStatusOutcome:126`) are package-level maps now (`responseMembers`, `profileNames`, `statusStates`), each consulted by a membership check, so the existing census derives them with no scanner change. Each carries a pinned-document derivation (`TestResponseMembersAreDerivedFromSpec` from the two 7.2 envelope sentences with `ok = true/false` normalized, `TestProfileNamesAreDerivedFromSpec` from the two 7.7 profile sentences with exactly-one-span guards, `TestStatusStatesAreDerivedFromSpec` from the 7.5 ProviderTransactionStatus state span), a census registration (19 → 22 vocabularies, both directions), and a production entry-point refusal row (envelope/`bogus` via DecodeResponse, `ProfileMapping(codex, bogus)`, bogus status state via DecodeStatusOutcome). `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` pins the residue: every production switch must be a classified dispatch (the one remaining switch dispatches on an already-validated state), so a new switch-shaped gate fails until classified. The \"closes the class by construction\" header now states the derived shapes plus this guard instead of an unstated-empty residue.\n26|- FIX (F2, blocking): `ExecRunner` discarded judgeable results through two races on `Host.Call`'s primary path. (a) `return Result{}, writeErr` before stdout was ever considered: an EPIPE racing the plugin's exit threw away valid correlated frames. (b) Found during this rework by driving `Run` directly (2 of 20 crash-script iters returned `read |0: file already closed`): `Wait` closes `StdoutPipe`/`StderrPipe` read ends after seeing the process exit, racing a drain still in flight — this, not EPIPE, is what misclassified the stdin-draining `exit 3` fixture. Fix per the file's own comments: judge whenever possible (non-empty stdout governs; empty stdout with a known exit classifies the crash through the Result), surface write/close/wait failures only with empty stdout and no known exit, and drain over `os.Pipe` pairs owned by `Run` so no later Close can interrupt a drain. New tests `TestExecRunnerKeepsValidFrameWhenPluginIgnoresStdin` (200 calls, zero discards) and `TestExecRunnerClassifiesCrashExitDeterministically` (50 crash calls, all `plugin exited without a response`): both FAIL on the pre-fix runner (2/200 frames discarded; crash misclassified as `runner reported no result`, each verified by swapping the pre-fix `runner.go` back with sha256-verified restore) and pass post-fix.\n27|- FLAKE BOUND: post-fix `go test ./internal/provhost/ -count=1` 30/30 green in two 15-run chunks (pre-fix: 3 red in 50 per the reviewer). The two F2 loops above are the deterministic pins; the old single-shot `TestExecRunnerReportsCrashExit` stays as a third witness.\n28|- EVIDENCE: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/provhost/` exit 0; gofmt clean; `go test ./... -count=1` green (15 packages); provhost `-race` green; provhost cover 86.5% → 86.0% (new judge/pipe branches). Widening mutants re-planted against the new maps (envelope/profile/status `\"bogus\"`, plus an unclassified-switch plant): each dies three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point row — with cp-aside/sha256 restores; the one vacuous-green run in the sequence (a gofmt-realigned anchor that planted nothing) was caught by the grep-plant assertion and re-run with the corrected anchor.\n29|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n30|\n(more lines below)"}}}
